      ⍝ Bugs28 #34 regression: A LO.RO B with a non-scalar LO (e.g. ,)
      ⍝ whose per-item reduction yields a nested scalar was wrongly
      ⍝ enclosed one level too deep (Bif_OPER2_INNER.cc used
      ⍝ V2->is_simple_scalar() -- rank 0 AND depth 0 -- to decide
      ⍝ between copying V2's cell directly vs. wrapping it in a new
      ⍝ PointerCell; that test is false for an already-nested scalar,
      ⍝ so V2 got wrapped *again*). Fixed by testing V2->is_scalar()
      ⍝ (rank 0, any depth) instead: any scalar's sole cell, simple or
      ⍝ itself a PointerCell, is copied as-is; only a genuine
      ⍝ (rank > 0) array needs a fresh wrapping PointerCell. See also
      ⍝ the J,.+P/≡J,.+P/4⎕CR J,.+P case earlier in this file, whose
      ⍝ expected output changed for the same reason.
      ⍝
      Z←1 2 3,.,4 5 6 ⋄ 2 ⎕TF 'Z'
Z←⊂6⍴1 2 3 4 5 6

      ⍝ control: a user-defined (lambda) LO was already correct
      ]FILE_CTL SKIP_APL2   ⍝ lambdas are a GNU APL extension
      Z←1 2 3{⍺,⍵}.,4 5 6 ⋄ 2 ⎕TF 'Z'
Z←⊂6⍴1 2 3 4 5 6

      ]FILE_CTL NO_SKIP
      ≡(1 2)(3 4)+.×(5 6)(7 8)
2

