      ⍝ Bugs28 #38 regression: A f.g B with an empty frame built the
      ⍝ fill result's structure (shape/nesting) correctly via RO's own
      ⍝ eval_fill_AB(), but never converted its actual cell VALUES to
      ⍝ a type-correct default -- e.g. 5 (RO's real result on the
      ⍝ actual fill args) leaked into the prototype instead of 0, and
      ⍝ 'a' 'b' (real characters) leaked in instead of spaces one
      ⍝ level down inside a nested fill result. Fixed in
      ⍝ Bif_OPER2_INNER::fill(): set_ravel_Value() + to_type(false)
      ⍝ (recurses through any nested PointerCell; false because a fill
      ⍝ result can legitimately be character and must stay character),
      ⍝ mirroring the OUTER product fix for the same class of bug.
      ⍝
      Z←(0 3⍴0)+.{⍺+⍵}3 2⍴5 ⋄ 2 ⎕TF 'Z'
Z←0 2⍴0

      ]FILE_CTL SKIP_APL2   ⍝ lambdas are a GNU APL extension
      ((0 3⍴0)+.{⍺+⍵}3 2⍴5)≡0 2⍴0
1

